{{!-- The share row — used bare in the post footer and boxed by
widgets/share.hbs.

FOUR actions, not seven. The row used to carry X, LinkedIn,
Facebook, email, copy, Claude and ChatGPT, which in a 260px rail
read as a wall of grey squares nobody parsed. What survived: the
two networks this audience actually posts to, the one action that
always works (copy), and the one that is genuinely useful on a
learning site (hand the page to an AI and ask about it). Facebook,
email and the second AI link were the ones pulling weight
nowhere.

Social intents are plain URLs, no scripts; the copy button is the
one bit that needs JS (assets/js/share.js, delegated so this
partial can render anywhere without its own listener). "Ask
Claude" opens a fresh chat pre-filled with the post's link — the
documented ?q= new-chat parameter, no API key, no script.
Context: the post. --}}
<div class="share-row">
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url={{url absolute="true"}}"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{t "Share on LinkedIn"}}" title="{{t "Share on LinkedIn"}}">{{> "icons/linkedin"}}</a>

    <a href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text={{encode title}}&url={{url absolute="true"}}"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{t "Share on X"}}" title="{{t "Share on X"}}">{{> "icons/x"}}</a>

    <button type="button" class="share-copy" data-copy-link="{{url absolute="true"}}" aria-label="{{t "Copy link"}}" title="{{t "Copy link"}}">
        <span class="share-copy-icon">{{> "icons/link-icon"}}</span>
        <span class="share-copy-done">{{> "icons/check-circle"}}</span>
    </button>

    <a href="https://claude.ai/new?q={{encode "Read this and tell me what stands out: "}}{{encode (url absolute="true")}}"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{t "Ask Claude about this"}}" title="{{t "Ask Claude about this"}}" class="share-ai">{{> "icons/sparkles"}}</a>
</div>
